messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2024,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2025,
      "event": "AI automates majority of knowledge work",
      "detail": "Advanced AI systems displace millions of white-collar jobs in coding, law, and administration, forcing rapid economic restructuring and debates over universal basic income."
    },
    {
      "year": 2028,
      "event": "Global temperature permanently exceeds 1.5°C",
      "detail": "Annual average temperature breaches 1.5°C above pre-industrial levels, locking in accelerated ice sheet melt and extreme weather patterns."
    },
    {
      "year": 2030,
      "event": "World population peaks at approximately 10.4 billion",
      "detail": "Demographic transition completes in most nations; population begins a long-term decline as fertility rates fall below replacement in nearly all countries."
    },
    {
      "year": 2035,
      "event": "Commercial fusion power becomes viable",
      "detail": "Private and public fusion reactors achieve sustained net energy gain, beginning deployment that gradually displaces fossil fuels in grid electricity."
    },
    {
      "year": 2040,
      "event": "Artificial general intelligence is achieved or approached",
      "detail": "AI systems match or exceed human capability across most cognitive domains; alignment, safety, and control become the central geopolitical challenges of the century."
    },
    {
      "year": 2045,
      "event": "First permanent human settlement established on Mars",
      "detail": "A base housing over 100 people achieves self-sufficiency in water and oxygen, marking humanity's transition to a multi-planetary species."
    },
    {
      "year": 2050,
      "event": "Cell-cultured meat and precision fermentation dominate protein markets",
      "detail": "Lab-grown and fermented proteins become cheaper than animal agriculture, leading to the collapse of industrial factory farming in developed economies."
    },
    {
      "year": 2055,
      "event": "Gene editing eliminates major infectious and hereditary diseases",
      "detail": "CRISPR-based therapies and vaccines eradicate malaria, HIV, and most single-gene disorders in wealthy nations, dramatically increasing healthy life expectancy."
    },
    {
      "year": 2060,
      "event": "One meter of sea level rise forces mass coastal retreat",
      "detail": "Hundreds of millions of people relocate from low-lying coastal zones; cities like Miami, Shanghai, and Jakarta either build massive sea walls or are partially abandoned."
    },
    {
      "year": 2065,
      "event": "Longevity escape velocity is achieved for humans",
      "detail": "Medical interventions increase life expectancy faster than time passes, allowing treated individuals to gain more than one year of life per calendar year."
    },
    {
      "year": 2070,
      "event": "Autonomous AI manages global critical infrastructure",
      "detail": "Power grids, supply chains, and transportation networks operate with minimal human oversight, increasing efficiency but creating systemic fragility risks."
    },
    {
      "year": 2075,
      "event": "Global fertility rate drops below 1.5 children per woman",
      "detail": "Demographic decline accelerates; automation and AI are required to maintain economic output as the working-age population shrinks in most nations."
    },
    {
      "year": 2080,
      "event": "First permanent orbital habitats house thousands",
      "detail": "O'Neill cylinders or rotating habitats in Earth orbit provide microgravity manufacturing and residential space, beginning the industrialization of space."
    },
    {
      "year": 2085,
      "event": "Global treaty establishes governance over existential technologies",
      "detail": "Following a near-miss involving nuclear standoff, engineered pathogens, or rogue AI, nations create an enforcement-capable body to regulate dangerous research."
    },
    {
      "year": 2090,
      "event": "Asteroid mining creates a trillion-dollar space economy",
      "detail": "Near-Earth asteroids are harvested for platinum-group metals, water, and rare earth elements, ending terrestrial resource scarcity and enabling large-scale space construction."
    },
    {
      "year": 2095,
      "event": "Stratospheric aerosol geoengineering begins",
      "detail": "Solar radiation management is deployed to offset warming, sparking intense international conflict over who controls the global thermostat and regional side effects."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "Automation provides post-scarcity basic goods on Earth",
      "detail": "Earth's population stabilizes around 9 billion; robotic labor and AI manage production, allowing most humans to pursue leisure, art, or scientific endeavors."
    },
    {
      "year": 2120,
      "event": "Brain-computer interfaces become mainstream",
      "detail": "Non-invasive neural links allow direct thought-to-computer communication, revolutionizing education, creativity, and human-computer collaboration."
    },
    {
      "year": 2150,
      "event": "Mind uploading creates the first digital consciousnesses",
      "detail": "Successful whole-brain emulation produces digital minds granted legal personhood in several jurisdictions, blurring the line between biological and artificial persons."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "Mars achieves self-sufficiency with one million inhabitants",
      "detail": "The Martian colony produces its own food, fuel, and manufactured goods, operating as an independent economy and backup for Earth civilization."
    },
    {
      "year": 2250,
      "event": "Interstellar probe arrives at Proxima Centauri",
      "detail": "A laser-propelled nanocraft launched around 2200 reaches the nearest star system, transmitting data and confirming the viability of interstellar travel."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "Space-based solar power provides majority of Earth's energy",
      "detail": "Orbital solar arrays beam microwave energy to rectennas on Earth, delivering clean baseload power and reducing terrestrial fossil fuel use to near zero."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "Supervolcano or asteroid impact causes global agricultural collapse",
      "detail": "A natural catastrophe blocks sunlight for several years; humanity survives through underground agriculture, stored food reserves, and off-world food production on Mars and orbital habitats."
    },
    {
      "year": 2500,
      "event": "First permanent settlement established outside the solar system",
      "detail": "A generation ship or vessel using suspended animation arrives at a nearby star, establishing humanity's first truly independent interstellar colony."
    },
    {
      "year": 2700,
      "event": "Genetic and cybernetic divergence causes speciation",
      "detail": "Distinct human-derived lineages emerge—unmodified 'baseline' humans, genetically enhanced humans, and fully cybernetic post-humans—with limited interbreeding and separate societies."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "Construction begins on a Dyson swarm around the Sun",
      "detail": "Humanity begins harvesting a significant fraction of the Sun's total energy output using millions of solar collectors, powering vast computational and industrial projects."
    },
    {
      "year": 3500,
      "event": "Post-biological entities become the dominant form of humanity",
      "detail": "Digital minds, uploaded consciousnesses, and AI descendants outnumber biological humans; 'humanity' is now primarily a post-biological civilization."
    },
    {
      "year": 4000,
      "event": "Earth becomes uninhabitable due to solar brightening",
      "detail": "The Sun's increased luminosity raises Earth's temperature beyond survivable limits without massive climate engineering; permanent evacuation to outer solar system habitats and other stars is completed."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "Humanity colonizes hundreds of star systems",
      "detail": "Relativistic ships, generation vessels, and uploaded minds traveling at near-light speed have established a multi-stellar civilization spanning a significant portion of the galaxy."
    },
    {
      "year": 6000,
      "event": "Stellar engineering (star lifting) begins",
      "detail": "Advanced civilization extracts mass from stars to extend their lifespans and harvest raw materials, fundamentally altering stellar evolution for energy and resources."
    },
    {
      "year": 7000,
      "event": "Entire star systems converted into Matrioshka brains",
      "detail": "Computational megastructures surround stars, running vast numbers of simulated minds and processing information at the theoretical limits of physics."
    },
    {
      "year": 8000,
      "event": "Galaxy-wide communication network established",
      "detail": "A network of quantum-entangled relays or laser chains spans thousands of light-years, creating a cohesive galactic civilization with shared culture and knowledge."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "Sun enters red giant phase",
      "detail": "The Sun expands and engulfs the inner planets; any remaining habitats in the solar system are abandoned in favor of other stars or artificial stellar habitats."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Humanity exists as a distributed post-biological civilization or has gone extinct",
      "detail": "If the species survived earlier bottlenecks, humanity now spans hundreds of star systems as diverse forms of intelligence; otherwise, the last humans or their descendants died out centuries earlier due to catastrophe."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "uncertain",
  "summary": "Humanity faces a critical bottleneck this century from climate change, unaligned AI, pandemics, and nuclear risk, with a substantial probability of extinction or permanent civilizational collapse before 2100. If we survive by becoming multi-planetary and establishing robust governance over transformative technologies, we likely evolve into a post-biological, multi-stellar civilization by the year 10000, though biological humans will have ceased to exist as a distinct category long before then."
}
